en:{headline:'Sound has a few surprises',subtitle:'Make a guess. Move a slider. See what your ears are trying to tell you.',intro:'3 little experiments<br>One small revelation at a time',notebook:'YOUR LAB NOTES',pause:'Audio paused',playing:'Audio playing',play:'Listen',stop:'Pause',volume:'Volume',headphones:'Start with device volume low',local:'Sound made in your browser · No uploads · No analytics',reset:'Reset this experiment ↺',footer:'For curious ears.',sources:'Science & sources',predict:'Make a guess',explore:'Try it yourself',reveal:'Reveal the science',guessHint:'A wrong guess is a very good place to start.',saved:'Prediction saved. Let your ears and eyes put it to the test.',locked:'Choose an answer to unlock the experiment.',revealLocked:'Change a setting to unlock the reveal.',next:'Next experiment →',done:'Three discoveries. Better ears.',doneNote:'Revisit any experiment and try a different setting.',correct:'You called it. Now you know why.',incorrect:'You found the little trick our ears can play.',picked:'Your prediction',theory:'Calculated illustration, not a live measurement',noAudio:'Audio could not start. Try Listen again, or open in a current Chrome, Safari or Firefox browser. You can still explore the graphs.',about:`<h2>About this little lab</h2><p>Three idealized signal experiments connect a change you hear with the science behind it. The graphs are calculated from the same controls, not microphone measurements. Audio starts only when you press Listen and pauses when you leave the page. Headphones work best for experiment three; device mono settings also affect the result.</p><p>Experiment one uses 220 Hz sine waves. Experiment two uses a fixed broadband noise source and one delayed copy. Experiment three uses an original synthesized melody and a high texture deliberately encoded as Side. Fixed attenuation leaves headroom; there is no automatic loudness compensation. At 0°, the summed signals use the same reference level as the original.</p><p>All sound is generated locally. No microphone, uploads or analytics scripts. Only the language preference is stored on this device. GitHub Pages serves the files and may keep ordinary access logs.</p><p>References: <a href="https://learningsynths.ableton.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ableton Learning Synths</a> · <a href="https://www.dsprelated.com/freebooks/pasp/Comb_Filters.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Julius O. Smith: Comb Filters</a> · <a href="https://www.dpamicrophones.com/dictionary/m/ms-recording/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DPA: Mid/Side</a> · <a href="https://www.ableton.com/en/live-manual/12/live-audio-effect-reference/#utility" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ableton Utility</a></p>`}
